% jfb 1
$$\int \frac{\text{d} x}{a x + b} = \frac{1}{a} \ln |a x + b| + C$$

---
## $\Gamma _0 = \alpha _0: x \in \mathbb{R}, \langle\text{static}\rangle\ a \in \mathbb{R}, \langle\text{static}\rangle\ b \in \mathbb{R}$

$\mathbf{ctx}\ \langle \text{换元法} \rangle u = a x + b$
$\color{Grey} \text{d} u = a \ \text{d} x$
$\text{d} x = \frac{1}{a} \ \text{d} u$

## $\Gamma _1 = \alpha _1: \alpha _0 + \text{换元法}$

$\int \frac{\text{d} x}{a x + b}$
$= \frac{1}{a} \int \frac{\text{d} u}{u}$
---
$[\mathbb{R}::int]$
$\mathbf{ori}\ C \in \mathbb R$
$= \frac{1}{a} \ln |u| + \color{Cyan} C$

## $\Gamma _1 = \Gamma _0 + \langle 换元法 \rangle$

$= \frac{1}{a} \ln |a x + b| + C$
